# FCR Payload conventions

Public site copy is English. Admin dashboard chrome is English by default with Italian as a second UI language; field names stay English `label`. No `localization` / `localized: true`. Follow `.cursor/rules/admin-italian.mdc`.

## Admin groups

Keep the sidebar short for non-expert editors. Prefer hub + hide over one big bucket.

- **Conferences** (`group` via `adminGroups.conferences`) — only **Conferences** / **Conferenze** in the nav. Nested edition content (`conference-days`, `agenda-items`, `appendices`, `abstracts`) stays `admin.hidden: true` and is edited via joins/tabs on the conference.
- **People and organisations** / **Persone e organizzazioni** — People, Institutions (cross-edition directories).
- **Content** / **Contenuti** — Media, Users (and similar site infrastructure).
- **References** / **Riferimenti** — seeded lookups (`countries`, `italian-regions`, `abstract-statuses`). Keep them visible here, not mixed with edition or directory collections.
- **Site** / **Sito** — Active conference and Conference archive use custom nav links and dashboard cards (`afterNavLinks` / `beforeDashboard`). **Edit active edition** / **Modifica edizione attiva** sits ungrouped at the top of the nav (`beforeNavLinks`) and dashboard, with a pencil control, when an active conference is set. **Publishing guide** / **Guida per chi pubblica** (`/docs`) is a dashboard banner only; it is not a Payload global and does not sit in Site. Footer stays in Globals as **Footer** / **Piè di pagina**. Do not put globals into Conferences.

Collection slugs are plural (`conferences`). Global slugs are singular (`footer`).

## Field editors

### Basic rich text (`basicLexical`)

Bold, italic, strikethrough, underline, superscript, subscript, inline code, ordered/unordered lists, indent, blockquote, horizontal rule, headings h3–h6, links. No h1/h2, align, uploads, checklists, or blocks unless asked.

Use for short formatted fields (names, location notes, appendix text). Prefer `@/fields/basicLexical`.

### Flexible description (`flexibleLexical`)

Full Payload Lexical defaults without checklists (headings, lists, align, indent, blockquote, links, relationships, uploads, inline code, HR) plus MediaBlock, tables (`EXPERIMENTAL_TableFeature`), fixed toolbar, and text colors (`TextStateFeature`). Prefer `@/fields/flexibleLexical`.

## Admin UX

- Tabs for major sections (bilingual labels, e.g. Overview / Panoramica, Venue / Sede, Public listing / Scheda pubblica). Field `label`s inside tabs stay English.
- Rows + `admin.width` for related small fields (year/logo, colors, city/country).
- Sidebar for slug, publishedAt, and derived/read-only helpers (e.g. plain `title`).
- Public listing tab (conferences): one tab for non-expert editors. Group `meta` with the `@payloadcms/plugin-seo` pattern (`OverviewField`, title/image/description, `PreviewField`). Group `geo` for optional AI-citation fields (`summary`, `primaryEntity`, `keyFacts`). No FAQs (no public FAQ UI). Field names stay English; tab/group `label`s and `admin.description` are bilingual (`copy(en, it)`). Emit JSON-LD `Event`/`Place` on public pages from venue + days + geo; `dateModified` comes from document `updatedAt`. Do not duplicate venue or listing fields.
- Always add `slug` when the collection is public-facing. Prefer `slugField` with a sensible `slugify` (e.g. year + title). Keep slugs unique; allow manual override.

## Public conference URLs

- Active conference (global `active-conference`) is the site root `/`.
- Past editions with `publicArchive: true` are at `/archive/{slug}` (managed via Conference archive global).
- Active edition slug under `/archive/...` redirects to `/`.
- Content overlays (abstract modal, photo gallery, …) are query params on that path. Follow `.cursor/rules/public-overlays.mdc`.

## Derived title from rich-text name

When display name is rich text:

1. Store formatted value in `name` (richText).
2. Auto-fill plain `title` via `beforeChange` using `convertLexicalToPlaintext` from `@payloadcms/richtext-lexical/plaintext`.
3. `useAsTitle: 'title'`; slug/SEO use `title`. Show `title` read-only in sidebar.

## Colors

Hex text fields with Payload custom Field `@/fields/color/ColorField`. UI components live under `src/components/admin/ui` (shadcn admin path), not `src/components/ui`.

## Ordering (`orderable`)

Manual display order is a first-class requirement. Prefer Payload’s built-in `orderable` (fractional `_order`), not a custom numeric `sort` / `order` field.

- **Collections** that are listed/ordered on the frontend (speakers, sponsors, schedule items, and similar): set `orderable: true` by default.
- **Join fields** when related docs need a custom order within the parent: set `orderable: true` on the join.
- **Frontend / Local API**: always fetch with `sort: '_order'` (or the join’s order field) so admin drag-and-drop matches the site.
- **Array / blocks fields**: order is already preserved by Payload; no `orderable` flag. Do not add a separate order field inside array rows unless there is a real nested-list need.
- Skip `orderable` only when order is purely derived (e.g. by date, year, title) and editors must not control sequence.

## New event collections

- File under `src/collections/<Name>/index.ts` (or single file if tiny).
- Pick the group by role: edition-scoped → `Conferenze` (usually `hidden` + join from conference); directories → `Persone e organizzazioni`; seeded lookups → `Riferimenti`.
- `orderable: true` when the collection is an ordered list for the FE (default for ordered FE lists unless order is date/title-driven).
- Access: authenticated write; `authenticatedOrPublished` (or `anyone`) for public read when drafts exist.
- Prefer drafts/versions when content is published to the frontend.
- Register in `payload.config.ts`; extend SEO `generateTitle` / `generateURL` when SEO fields are present.
- Venue coordinates: use two `number` fields (`longitude`, `latitude`) in a row — not Payload `point`. `point` + postgres drafts is broken in Payload 3.90 (`ST_GeomFromGeoJSON` on raw `[lng, lat]`). Do not name coordinates `location` if that is venue notes rich text.

## Editor guide

User-facing CMS or public-site features must be documented in the bilingual Nextra guide (`content/en/*.mdx` and `content/it/*.mdx`, `/docs`). Follow `.cursor/rules/editor-docs.mdc`.
